      "text": "Let's solve the problem step by step.\n\n1. **Identify Key Points and Angles:**\n   - \\(AB\\) is the diameter of the circle centered at \\(O\\).\n   - \\(E\\) is a point on the circle.\n   - \\(C\\) is the intersection of the tangent at \\(B\\) and the tangent at \\(E\\).\n   - \\(D\\) is the intersection of the line \\(AE\\) and the tangent at \\(B\\).\n   - \\(\\angle BAE = 43^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Use Properties of Tangents and Secants:**\n   - Since \\(AB\\) is the diameter, \\(\\angle AEB = 90^\\circ\\) (angle subtended by the diameter).\n   - The tangent at \\(B\\) is perpendicular to \\(AB\\), so \\(\\angle OBE = 90^\\circ\\).\n   - The tangent at \\(E\\) is perpendicular to \\(OE\\), so \\(\\angle OEE' = 90^\\circ\\), where \\(E'\\) is a point on the tangent at \\(E\\) such that \\(OE'\\) is perpendicular to \\(OE\\).\n\n3. **Analyze the Angles:**\n   - Since \\(E'\\) is on the tangent at \\(E\\), \\(\\angle OEE' = 90^\\circ\\).\n   - \\(\\angle OBB' = 90^\\circ - \\angle BEO = 90^\\circ - \\angle BAE = 90^\\circ - 43^\\circ = 47^\\circ\\) (since \\(B\\) and \\(E'\\) are endpoints of the same tangent line at \\(E\\)).\n   - Therefore, \\(\\angle OBE = \\angle OBE' = 90^\\circ\\).\n\n4. **Determine \\(\\angle CED\\):**\n   - \\(\\angle CED\\) is the angle between the tangents at \\(B\\) and \\(E\\).\n   - The angle between two tangents at a point outside the circle is equal to the angle subtended by the chord connecting the points of contact of the tangents at the point of contact to the chord.\n   - Therefore, \\(\\angle CED = 2 \\times \\angle BEO = 2 \\times 43^\\circ = 86^\\circ\\).\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle CED\\) is \\(\\boxed{86}\\).",
